1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,960
Sir Lancelot was among Arthur’s greatest knights,

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:06,620
celebrated for courage and loyalty.

3
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,060
Yet his devotion to Queen Guinevere grew

4
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:12,280
into a love that threatened the court

5
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:12,960
itself.

6
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:16,740
Their relationship could not remain private forever.

7
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,200
In many Arthurian tellings,

8
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,740
the very bonds that made Camelot glorious

9
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:24,660
became tangled in betrayal.

10
00:00:25,467 --> 00:00:27,440
When the affair was revealed,

11
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:30,700
conflict erupted among people who had once

12
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:32,380
fought shoulder to shoulder.

13
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:35,077
Loyalty divided the Round Table.

14
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,840
Lancelot acted to save Guinevere,

15
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:42,300
but the rescue intensified the war within

16
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:45,460
Arthur’s kingdom. Each choice made the next

17
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,100
disaster harder to prevent.

18
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:50,340
While Arthur pursued the conflict,

19
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:53,220
other enemies exploited the division.

20
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:56,880
Camelot’s downfall arrived not through lack of

21
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:59,335
strength, but through broken trust.

22
00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:03,360
Later retellings remember not one villain,

23
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:05,580
but a tragic knot of love,

24
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:07,160
honor, and duty.

25
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:10,820
A perfect court could not contain imperfect

26
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:11,800
human hearts.
